---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SplitSection from "../components/SplitSection.astro";
import AboutIntro from "../components/AboutIntro.astro";
import Appearances from "../components/Appearances.astro";
---

<Base title="About Niko Karppinen" description="Niko Karppinen is an SEO and analytics consultant working across digital measurement, technical implementation and practical digital systems." schemaPageType="about">
  <AboutIntro />

  <SplitSection id="approach" variant="about">
    <Fragment slot="title">
      <h2>How I approach work</h2>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="copy">
      <p>
        Good systems should make the next decision clearer. That is the test I
        come back to, whether I am looking at a measurement plan, a site
        structure, or a tracking implementation.
      </p>
      <p>
        My work often sits where SEO, analytics, content, tracking, and technical
        implementation meet. I tend to connect information across those areas
        instead of treating each one as a separate problem. Sometimes that also
        means asking whether the original problem has been framed correctly.
      </p>
      <p>
        When a subject is abstract, I use concrete examples, analogies, and small
        working models to make it easier to inspect. I would rather build
        something that can be tested than deliver a vague recommendation that
        sounds finished.
      </p>
      <p>
        AI can help apply a clear process more consistently. It cannot repair
        unclear ownership, unreliable source data, or a process nobody
        understands.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </SplitSection>

  <SplitSection id="values" variant="about">
    <Fragment slot="title">
      <h2>What I care about</h2>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="copy">
      <p>
        I care about clarity, trust, and useful structure: measurement that
        supports real decisions rather than producing more numbers to maintain.
      </p>
      <p>
        Good work should leave people with enough context to judge what matters
        and enough structure to act on it. Tools can surface patterns, but human
        judgment still decides what matters for the customer, the business, and
        the brand.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </SplitSection>

  <SplitSection id="background" variant="about">
    <Fragment slot="title">
      <h2>Background</h2>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="copy">
      <p>
        I have worked with SEO, analytics, and digital marketing since 2017.
        Over the years, I have worked with ecommerce businesses,
        telecommunications companies, public-sector organisations, consumer
        brands, and B2B companies.
      </p>
      <p>
        My work has included technical SEO audits, analytics implementations,
        consent and tracking setups, website redesign support, measurement
        planning, dashboard development, and search-driven site structure
        planning.
      </p>
      <p>
        I have long been interested in the relationship between technology,
        content, structure, and storytelling. I have also written short-film
        screenplays — not as a professional credential, but because I enjoy
        working out how ideas, pacing, and communication fit together.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </SplitSection>

  <SplitSection id="outside-work" variant="about">
    <Fragment slot="title">
      <h2>Outside work</h2>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="copy">
      <p>
        Outside work, I spend a fair amount of time with films, anime, and
        story-driven single-player games. Alan Wake and Metal Gear Solid are
        particular favourites. I am drawn to stories with strong structure,
        atmosphere, and slightly unusual worlds.
      </p>
      <p>
        Comics are another constant, especially Batman and Teenage Mutant Ninja
        Turtles. I like strong concepts and worlds with their own internal
        logic.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also dance Cuban salsa and locking. Both combine structure, rhythm,
        practice, and improvisation. They are also good at making overconfidence
        visible very quickly.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </SplitSection>

  <Appearances />
</Base>
